                <pb facs="0462" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg448"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Monroe, Secretary
                        of State, to Mr. Robinson</hi>.</head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                        State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1814-02-17"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">February</hi> 17, 1814</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is reason to believe that General
                    Toledo, late commander of the revolutionists in the Spanish province of Texas,
                    and General Humbert, a Frenchman, *act in concert and are engaged with Doctor
                    Robinson. It is my wish, therefore, that the instructions in relation to him,
                    communicated in my letter to you of the 14th instant, may be extended to them.
                        <seg type="margin">[10]</seg></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES MONROE.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tully Robinson</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
